  "interpretation": "Concurrency alone cannot explain the failures: the 12-, 24- and 32-stream sustained controls all completed their expected bytes without reconnecting, while each corresponding synchronized workload exited on a /data read reset with no final sample. One and four streams completed in both workloads. The workloads also differ in setup and reuse; the archive cannot isolate just the barrier, prove credit starvation, locate the failing request within the executable, or supply mixed-load p95/p99 for failed runs. One diagnostic per count and shape does not identify a reliable concurrency threshold. Keep bulk vsock gated on per-stream delivery and backpressure evidence under synchronized first responses."
